course: dictionary
lesson: 11343
title: Same letter, different names
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change from place to place. The same letter can have a different name in America and in Britain. «The letter Z is "zed" in Britain, Ireland, Canada, Australia and most English-speaking places, and "zee" in the USA.» So zee is the American word, and zed is the word most people in the UK, Ireland and Australia use.
explain: Some words also have an informal meaning. Zees, or z's, is informal for sleep. In «catch some z's», it means having a nap or going to sleep. Cartoons show sleep with zzz, which is why the letter z stands for snoring. Check the sentence: if sleep fits, you have the right meaning.
explain: When a word has more than one meaning, look at the words around it. In a spelling lesson, zee means the letter. After «catch some», zees means sleep. The context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Zee is the name of the letter Z in American English.
fact: Most of the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand say zed for the letter Z.
fact: Zees, or z's, is informal for sleep, as in «catch some z's».
fact: Cartoons often show sleep as zzz, because snoring sounds like a long buzzing.
fact: A dictionary tells you which meaning, and which country, a word belongs to.
exercise: In «The letter Z is "zed" in Britain, Ireland, Canada, Australia and most English-speaking places, and "zee" in the USA», which country says zee? | Ireland | Britain | *The USA | Australia
exercise: Mum says, «I need to catch some z's before the film.» What does z's mean here? | Zero | Letters of the alphabet | *Sleep | Zebras
exercise: Why do cartoons show zzz? | *To show someone is asleep or snoring | To show a loud shout | To show a letter sound | To show someone is angry
test: Which word is the American name for the letter Z? | Zebra | Zed | *Zee | Zoom
test: What does zees mean in the phrase «catch some zees»? | Zoo | Zero | Letters | *Sleep
exam: Which sentence uses zee as the name of a letter? | «The cartoon showed zzz.» | «The zebra ran across the field.» | «I need to catch some z's.» | *«In the USA, the letter Z is called zee.»
